What brcmfmac's transmit asks of a buffer (HakiOS): only that it has room for the driver's header, not that it is
not a clone, which LinuxKPI cannot tell (lx-tx.patch). And the data path's first steps said: the flow rings asked
for and made, the first frames posted and the firmware's status for each.
--- a/brcmfmac/core.c
+++ b/brcmfmac/core.c
@@ -328,8 +328,13 @@
 		goto done;
 	}
 
-	/* Make sure there's enough writeable headroom */
-	if (skb_headroom(skb) < drvr->hdrlen || skb_header_cloned(skb)) {
+	/*
+	 * Make sure there's enough writeable headroom. (HakiOS) LinuxKPI's skb_header_cloned() is a TODO that says
+	 * true of every buffer, and its pskb_expand_head() always fails, so every frame sent was dropped here ("failed
+	 * to expand headroom"; the four-way handshake's message 2 among them). Nothing here clones a buffer, and the
+	 * frames given to the driver (lx_cfg.c's frame_send()) leave room for its header: only too little room counts.
+	 */
+	if (skb_headroom(skb) < drvr->hdrlen) {
 		head_delta = max_t(int, drvr->hdrlen - skb_headroom(skb), 0);
 
 		brcmf_dbg(INFO, "%s: %s headroom\n", brcmf_ifname(ifp),
